{"D:\\wt\\sgardenmole\\vlog\\sgardenmole\\voz\\b013_t1.wav": {"text": "And remember, in very dry summers, moles go deep and you see nothing. Then in the fall rains, they come up again. So start again every fall. My mother kept a little calendar by the back door. And on the first rainy weekend of October, she wrote one word on it, mogara, so she would not forget. I do the same thing on my kitchen calendar now, in pencil. And every year it reminds me of her. Now, the fixing. When the moles are gone, rake the hills flat, step down the soft tunnels so your ankles are safe, and throw a little grass seed on the bare spots with a handful of good soil. Water gently every day for a week. In one month nobody will know they were there. Keep a little of the soil from the hills in a bucket, because it is the finest, softest soil in the whole yard. My mother used it for her seedlings in the spring, and she said the mogara had done her digging for her.", "words": [{"w": " And", "s": 0.0, "e": 0.12}, {"w": " remember,", "s": 0.12, "e": 1.02}, {"w": " in", "s": 1.02, "e": 1.12}, {"w": " very", "s": 1.12, "e": 1.46}, {"w": " dry", "s": 1.46, "e": 1.86}, {"w": " summers,", "s": 1.86, "e": 2.54}, {"w": " moles", "s": 2.54, "e": 2.7}, {"w": " go", "s": 2.7, "e": 3.0}, {"w": " deep", "s": 3.0, "e": 3.46}, {"w": " and", "s": 3.46, "e": 3.7}, {"w": " you", "s": 3.7, "e": 3.82}, {"w": " see", "s": 3.82, "e": 4.04}, {"w": " nothing.", "s": 4.04, "e": 4.94}, {"w": " Then", "s": 4.94, "e": 5.14}, {"w": " in", "s": 5.14, "e": 5.26}, {"w": " the", "s": 5.26, "e": 5.4}, {"w": " fall", "s": 5.4, "e": 5.72}, {"w": " rains,", "s": 5.72, "e": 6.2}, {"w": " they", "s": 6.2, "e": 6.3}, {"w": " come", "s": 6.3, "e": 6.52}, {"w": " up", "s": 6.52, "e": 6.7}, {"w": " again.", "s": 6.7, "e": 7.54}, {"w": " So", "s": 7.44, "e": 7.6}, {"w": " start", "s": 7.6, "e": 7.96}, {"w": " again", "s": 7.96, "e": 8.36}, {"w": " every", "s": 8.36, "e": 8.82}, {"w": " fall.", "s": 8.82, "e": 9.74}, {"w": " My", "s": 9.8